### Page 2 of 3

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
November 13, 2025
Jennifer Corso, Cheyenne MPO, presented the Connect 2050 Plan. The plan serves as the
federally required long-range plan for the Cheyenne Urbanized Area and is the update to the
PlanCheyenne Metropolitan Transportation and Future Land Use Plan. This plan outlines
the transportation needs through the year 2050.
Vice Chairman Watkins called the Public Hearing to order. No comments were received
and the hearing was closed and a motion and discussion called for. Commissioner Stadel
said he saw a list of everyone involved in this, was BOPU involved? Ms. Corso responded
that BOPU was not involved in this stage but they get involved when projects are further
along and in the design stage. Commissioner Casey asked if this was a shared expense
for the agencies. Ms Corso said that the MPO pays 90% with the County and City paying
5% each for the plans. MPO funding comes from the Transportation Enhancement Fund
from the federal government. Funding for the project themselves come from the
appropriate agency or developer who's project is being done.
Commissioner Tafoya moved, seconded by Commissioner Casey to
recommend approval of the CONNECT 2050 Plan to the Laramie County
Board of County Commissioners. Vote 4-0.
Casey, Stadel, Tafoya II, Watkins
Aye:
Caughey
Excused:
3.
Public Hearing regarding the amendment to the 2024 Edition of the
IRC Section R105.2 Work Exempt from Permit.
25 - 544
PC 11.13.25 Pkt
Attachments:
Justin Arnold reported that this amendment will change the footage of a single story
residential accessory structure from 200 to 400 square feet before a building permit
will be required. This will exempt shipping containers, sheds, and smaller carports
from building permits.
Vice Chairman Watkins called the public hearing open. Hearing no comments the
hearing was closed and a motion and discussion called for.
Commissioner Casey said he feels this is a no brainer and is an easy one to make a
motion and be confident we are doing the right thing.
Commissioner Casey moved, seconded by Commissioner Stadel to
recommend approval to the Laramie County Board of Commissioners to
amend the 2024 International Residential Code Section 105.2 - Work
Exempt from Permit. Vote 4-0.
Adjournment
The next meeting of the Planning Commission will be December 11, 2025 and will be the only meeting
in December. Having no further business the meeting was adjourned at 3:47 p.m.
